/-
  QBP.Foundations.Artin
  =====================

  PR-C2d of the Artin strategy (`docs/foundations/artin-strategy-2026-06-06.md`,
  lemma L5, the C2d row).  **The full Artin theorem at 𝕆 = `CDAlg ℝ 3`.**

  This is the final assembly chunk that closes **#474 AC2 (Artin)**.  All inputs
  are merged kernel theorems:

    * `ArtinCore.assoc_vanishes_on_span4` (C2a) — the associator `assoc`
      vanishes on the whole module span `span ℝ {1, x, y, x*y}`, proven by the
      complete 64-generator-triple discharge (L1 + alternativity-diag + L2
      survivor + flexibility) lifted through trilinearity.  **No** appeal to the
      Hurwitz / composition-algebra classification.
    * `ArtinSpan.mem_span4_of_mem_adjoin` (C2c) — every element of the genuine
      non-unital generated subalgebra `NonUnitalAlgebra.adjoin ℝ {x, y}` lies in
      `span ℝ {1, x, y, x*y}`, proven by direct 16-cell structure-constant
      multiplicative closure of the span (quadraticity + swap identity +
      alternativity) and `NonUnitalAlgebra.adjoin_le` minimality.  **No** appeal
      to classification.

  The assembly is three lines of theory: push all three of `u, v, w` from
  adjoin-membership to span4-membership (C2c), conclude `assoc u v w = 0` (C2a),
  and unfold `assoc u v w = (u*v)*w − u*(v*w)` to read off `(u*v)*w = u*(v*w)`.

  **Truth-in-labelling (Wilson W1 — gate item).**  This file genuinely proves
  Artin's theorem at the octonions: *every subalgebra of `CDAlg ℝ 3` generated by
  two elements is associative.*  The Lean object `NonUnitalAlgebra.adjoin ℝ {x,y}`
  IS the generated non-unital subalgebra (not a hand-picked monomial list), and
  the conclusion `(u*v)*w = u*(v*w)` for ALL `u v w` in it IS associativity of
  that subalgebra.  This is the FULL Artin theorem instantiated at the matrix
  cell, NOT a weakening.

  The proof is derived **from alternativity** (via the merged
  `octonion_alternative` / polarized-alternativity / flexibility lemmas), through
  the span route — there is **NO** appeal to Hurwitz's theorem, to the
  classification of composition algebras, or to "every 2-generated subalgebra of a
